"First, solve the inequality $|x| + 1 > 7$:\n\\[\n|x| > 6 \\implies -6 < x < 6.\n\\]\n\nNext, solve the inequality $|x+1| \\le 7$:\n\\[\n|x + 1| \\le 7 \\implies -8 \\le x \\le 6.\n\\]\n\nThe intersection of these two inequalities gives the values of $x$ that satisfy both conditions:\n\\[\n-6 < x < 6 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad -8 \\le x \\le 6 \\implies -3 \\le x \\le 3.\n\\]\n\nThe integers within this range are $-3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3$.\n\nThe sum of these integers is:\n\\[\n-3 + (-2) + (-1) + 0 + 1 + 2 + 3 = \\boxed{-2}.\n\n\\]"
