"The midpoint of a line segment with endpoints \\((x_1, y_1)\\) \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is given by the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2}, \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} \\right)\n\\]\n\nFor points \\( P(5, 3) \\) and \\( Q(-3, 6) \\):\n\n\\[\n\\left( \\frac{5 + (-3)}{2}, \\frac{3 + 6}{2} \\right) = \\left( \\frac{2}{2}, \\frac{9}{2} \\right) = (1, 4)\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the midpoint of \\(\\overline{PQ}\\) is \\(\\boxed{(1, 4)}\\)."
