"To evaluate \\(\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{5}}125\\), we can use the properties of logarithms. Specifically, we will use the property that \\(\\log_b a = \\frac{\\log_c a}{\\log b}\\).\n\nFirst, let's rewrite the expression using the change of base formula:\n\\[\n\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{5}}125 = \\frac{\\log 125}{\\log \\sqrt[3]{5}}\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that \\(\\log \\sqrt[3]{5} = \\frac{\\log 5}{3}\\). Therefore, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{5}}125 = \\frac{\\log 125}{\\frac{\\log 5}{3}} = \\frac{\\log 125}{\\log 5} \\cdot 3 = 3\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\log_{\\sqrt[3]{5}}125\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\)."
