"Let $a$, $b$, $c$, and $d$ be the times that Anna, Bertram, Carli, and David can hold their breath, respectively. We have the following equations:\n\n\\begin{align*}\nb+c+d&=3a\\\\\na+c+d&=4b\\\\\na+b+d&=2c\\\\\n8a+10b+6c&=\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 60=24.\n\\end{align*}\n\nAdding the first three equations, we get $3a+3b+3c+3d=8a+10b+6c$. Substituting this into the fourth equation, we get $3d=24$, so $d=\\frac{24}{3}$. The sum of the numerator and the denominator is $24+3=\\boxed{27}$."
