"Let \\( L \\) be the amount of money Lenny has. Then Larry has \\( \\frac{2}{5}L \\) dollars. The total amount of money they have together is $35, so we can write the equation:\n\n\\[ L + \\frac{2}{5}L = 35 \\]\n\nCombining like terms, we get:\n\n\\[ \\frac{7}{5}L = 35 \\]\n\nTo solve for \\( L \\), we multiply both sides by \\( \\frac{5}{7} \\):\n\n\\[ L = 35 \\times \\frac{5}{7} = 25 \\]\n\nSo, Lenny has $25. Larry has \\( \\frac{2}{5} \\times 25 = 10 \\) dollars. The difference in their amounts is:\n\n\\[ 25 - 10 = 15 \\]\n\nTherefore, Lenny has \\(\\boxed{15}\\) more dollars than Larry."
