"To find the value of \\( f(-2) \\) for the function \\( f(x) = 5x^2 + 3x + 4 \\), we substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the function and simplify.\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = 5(-2)^2 + 3(-2) + 4\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\( (-2)^2 \\):\n\n\\[\n(-2)^2 = 4\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply by 5:\n\n\\[\n5 \\cdot 4 = 20\n\\]\n\nThen, calculate \\( 3(-2) \\):\n\n\\[\n3(-2) = -6\n\\]\n\nFinally, add these results together with 4:\n\n\\[\n20 - 6 + 4 = 18\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( f(-2) \\) is \\(\\boxed{18}\\)."
